# Objects the parallel QEMU gate (ci_nightly.py --gate-workers N) runs
# afterwards, alone and in the shared selftests output (swap-and-test.sh,
# as with one worker). One name per line; '#' comments.

# prog_tests/fentry_attach.c:test_fentry_attach_stress attaches/detaches
# fentry programs to fentry_target while another thread runs it; under load
# the kernel hit an int3 Oops in the target (nightly/20261015-kvm).
fentry_recursive
fentry_recursive_target

# prog_tests/bpf_iter.c's task_vma subtest compares the bpf_d_path and
# dev:ino of test_progs's own mapping with /proc/self/maps. A file mapped
# through an overlay has the real layer file as vm_file, so under the
# overlay gate the iterator prints "/test_progs" on the layer's device and
# the subtest fails, for the C object too. Every bpf_iter_* object is
# consumed by that test.
